 "title": "Anvil Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: a metallic, struck melody: the clanking, hammered-metal lead of 80s industrial synth-pop, still in tune enough to play tunes with.\n\nHow it's built: two sine waves, the second an octave and a bit over a fourth higher, multiplied in a Ring Mod: the sum and difference tones ring like struck metal. MIX keeps some of the first sine, so the note is still heard. A struck envelope (quick decay to a low sustain), a Delay and a Reverb for the warehouse. Four voices.\n\nPlay: short melodic phrases, single notes, repeated hits.\n\nTweak: the second oscillator's TUNE (whole numbers are more in tune, odd values more metallic), the ring mod's MIX, the envelope's DECAY.",
